-- indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261106 (English 1682 words; Nepali 558 words; primary keyword in title, first paragraph, subheading)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261106', 'asia', 'India',
'Indian Bank Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 1,500 Posts, Apply by 25 November',
'इन्डियन बैंक अप्रेन्टिस भर्ती २०२६: १,५०० पद, २५ नोभेम्बरसम्म आवेदन',
'Indian Bank has opened 1,500 apprentice seats for 2026-27, with applications running from 5 to 25 November 2026 through the NATS portal. Graduates in any discipline can apply, the stipend is Rs 15,000 a month in metro and urban branches and Rs 12,300 in rural branches, and selection is by an online test followed by a local language test.',
'इन्डियन बैंकले आर्थिक वर्ष २०२६–२७ का लागि १,५०० अप्रेन्टिस पद खोलेको छ। ५ देखि २५ नोभेम्बर २०२६ सम्म एनएटीएस पोर्टलबाट आवेदन दिन सकिन्छ। मासिक भत्ता महानगरमा १५,००० र ग्रामीण क्षेत्रमा १२,३०० भारतीय रुपैयाँ छ।',
$$<p>Indian Bank has opened 1,500 apprentice seats for the financial year 2026-27, and applications run from 5 to 25 November 2026 through the National Apprenticeship Training Scheme (NATS) portal. The notification is the final updated advertisement for engagement of apprentices under the Apprentices Act, 1961, dated 4 November 2026, and every figure in this article comes from that document. It is a 12-month apprenticeship with a monthly stipend, not a permanent bank job, and that one fact decides whether it is worth your time.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Indian Bank Apprentice 2026-27</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Indian Bank, public sector bank, headquarters Chennai</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Apprentice</td></tr><tr><td>Total seats</td><td>1,500 (provisional)</td></tr><tr><td>Notification date</td><td>4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>5 to 25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>NATS 2.0 portal (nats.education.gov.in), via indianbank.bank.in careers page</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Graduation in any discipline, passed on or after 1 April 2022 and not later than 1 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>20 to 28 years as on 1 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly stipend</td><td>Rs 15,000 in metro and urban branches; Rs 12,300 in rural and semi-urban branches</td></tr><tr><td>Training duration</td><td>12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs 800 plus GST for most candidates; Rs 175 plus GST for SC, ST and PwBD</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Online test, then a local language test</td></tr></table>
<h2>Who can apply, and the graduation date that catches people out</h2>
<p>Any graduate can apply, with a date condition that matters more than the degree itself. You must have passed graduation on or after 1 April 2022 and not later than 1 November 2026, with the final result declared on or before 1 November 2026. A 2021 graduate cannot apply, even with a strong degree. A 2026 graduate whose result came out on 2 November cannot apply either. The advertisement is strict on both ends of that window, and it asks for proof of the result date at the document stage.</p>
<p>The age window is 20 to 28 years as on 1 November 2026. That means a date of birth between 2 November 1998 and 1 November 2006, both dates included. Relaxation follows Government of India rules: 5 years for SC and ST, 3 years for OBC non-creamy layer, 10 years for PwBD, and 5 years for people affected by the 1984 riots. Widows, divorced women and women legally separated who have not remarried get age concession up to 35 years for General and EWS, 38 for OBC and 40 for SC and ST.</p>
<p>Three more exclusions sit in the fine print. Anyone who has already done apprenticeship training anywhere, anyone currently doing it, and anyone whose earlier apprenticeship ended midway is out. One year or more of work experience after finishing your qualification also disqualifies you. And there is no reservation for ex-servicemen in this engagement. Before you touch the form, check two dates: your graduation result date and your date of birth. Those two decide eligibility before anything else in the process gets a look in.</p>
<h2>Where the 1,500 seats are</h2>
<p>Indian Bank has split the seats across all 30 states and union territories, and you apply for one state or UT only. Uttar Pradesh has the largest share at 285 seats, Tamil Nadu follows with 270, and West Bengal has 145. Andhra Pradesh has 85, Bihar 80, Maharashtra 70, Madhya Pradesh 65, Jharkhand 60, Telangana 46, Punjab 45, Kerala 44 and Odisha 42, with 263 seats spread across the other 18 states and union territories.</p>
<p>The category split across the 1,500 seats is 676 unreserved, 348 OBC, 252 SC, 142 EWS and 82 ST. The figures are provisional, and the bank can change them according to its actual requirement. Your home district gets first preference in the merit list for that district, and you can also pick two more neighbouring districts when you register. But the bank can post you to any district inside the state you pick, so choose the state where you can actually report for a year of branch training. Filing two applications for two states does not help: only the latest valid application is kept, and the fee paid on the others is forfeited.</p>
<h2>The exam is 100 questions in 60 minutes</h2>
<p>Selection has two stages, and the first is an online objective test of 100 questions for 100 marks, with a composite time of 60 minutes. Reasoning Aptitude carries 15 questions, Computer Knowledge 10, English Language 25, Quantitative Aptitude 25, and General Awareness with special reference to the Banking Industry 25. The test is held in major regional languages, except General English, which is in English. There are no minimum qualifying marks for any single section. You need the minimum aggregate marks the bank decides, with 5 percent relaxation on the aggregate for reserved category candidates.</p>
<p>The merit list is drawn state-wise and category-wise, in descending order of aggregate marks, and ties at the cut-off are broken by age, with the older candidate ranked higher. If the test runs in more than one session, scores are normalised with the equi-percentile method. A wait list is also drawn for each state and category. The bank may hold an interview, or it may skip it; the advertisement leaves that to its discretion. The advertisement names no exam date. Do not trust a date from a coaching site or a video thumbnail until the bank puts it on its own website.</p>
<p>The second stage is the Local Language Proficiency Test. You must be able to read, write, speak and understand one of the specified local languages of the state you applied for, and you pick that language when you apply. Hindi for Uttar Pradesh, Tamil for Tamil Nadu, Bengali for West Bengal, and so on down the list. If your 8th, 10th or 12th mark sheet shows you studied that language, you skip this test. If it does not, you sit the test after qualifying the online exam, and failing it ends the process. You appear for it in the state you applied for, at your own expense.</p>
<h2>How to apply on NATS without getting stuck</h2>
<p>The application lives in two places, and the order matters. First, register on the NATS 2.0 portal at nats.education.gov.in and complete your student profile to 100 percent. Only a complete profile can be used to apply, so do this before the last days. Note your Enrolment ID; the bank uses it for all later correspondence. Then find the vacancy titled Engagement of Apprentices in Indian Bank 2026 on the portal, or go through the careers page on indianbank.bank.in, and submit the application. Creating a NATS account alone is not an application. You have to apply against the advertised vacancy itself.</p>
<p>The fee is Rs 800 plus GST for most candidates. SC, ST and PwBD candidates pay Rs 175 plus GST. It is non-refundable, and you pay it online between 5 and 25 November 2026. Bank transaction charges for the online payment are yours to bear. Keep four documents ready before you start: a photograph, a signature, a left thumb impression, and a handwritten declaration, all scanned to the sizes in Annexure II of the advertisement. The declaration must be in your own handwriting, in English, and not in capital letters. A signature in capital letters is not accepted.</p>
<p>Read the nationality and eligibility conditions in the official notification before applying, since this is an Indian public sector bank engagement. Apply only through the NATS portal and the bank's own careers page, and never pay anyone who promises to get you a seat. Genuine recruitment never charges a fee to apply beyond the application fee named in the notification itself.</p>
<h2>What the stipend covers, and what it does not</h2>
<p>The stipend is Rs 15,000 a month in metro and urban branches, and Rs 12,300 a month in rural or semi-urban branches. In a metro branch the bank pays Rs 8,850 and the government pays Rs 6,150 through the apprenticeship portal. In a rural or semi-urban branch each side pays Rs 6,150. Apprentices get no other allowances or benefits, and the bank is exempt from EPF and ESI contributions for apprentices. Training runs 12 months. You get the bank holidays observed in the branch, plus one casual leave for each month of training, with no more than four casual leaves at a time.</p>
<p>You need more than 338 paid days inside those 12 months to qualify for the Certificate of Proficiency, which the Board of Apprenticeship Training (Southern Region) issues digitally through the NATS portal after a central assessment test. Daily hours match the bank's normal working hours, and there is no overtime. What the stipend does not carry matters as much as the figure. Apprentices are trainees, not bank employees. The contract ends after 12 months, and Indian Bank states plainly that it has no obligation to offer regular or contractual employment during or after the training. Completing the year does not create a claim to absorption.</p>
<p>So judge the year on its own terms. It is a year of paid training inside a public sector bank, with a stipend that covers living costs in most of the states on the list, and a certificate at the end that shows a year inside a government bank. It is not a back door into a permanent Indian Bank job, and anyone selling it as one is selling something the notification does not promise. A similar opening runs alongside this one: <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/nicl-graduate-apprentice-200-posts-20261106">National Insurance Company Limited has opened 200 Graduate Apprentice seats</a> for the same financial year, also through NATS, with applications closing on 18 November. That one has no exam at all: graduation marks decide it. It is worth comparing the two before you commit to one state in one of them. Those weighing an apprenticeship against other options can also compare it with other large apprentice intakes, such as the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rites-apprentice-281-posts-20261104">281 apprentice posts at RITES</a> listed on Growentix.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Indian Bank, final updated advertisement for engagement of apprentices for FY 2026-27, dated 4 November 2026, read 6 November 2026 from the official PDF on indianbank.bank.in, as reported by JobCareerUpdates at https://jobcareerupdates.in/blog/indian-bank-apprentice-recruitment-2026/ and Testbook at https://testbook.com/news/indian-bank-apprentice-recruitment-2026/ on the seats, dates, stipends, fees, exam pattern and eligibility conditions. Apply only through nats.education.gov.in.</small></p>
$$,
$$<p>इन्डियन बैंकले आर्थिक वर्ष २०२६–२७ का लागि १,५०० अप्रेन्टिस पद खोलेको छ। ४ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा प्रकाशित अन्तिम अद्यावधिक विज्ञापनअनुसार ५ देखि २५ नोभेम्बर २०२६ सम्म एनएटीएस पोर्टलबाट आवेदन दिन सकिन्छ। यो १२ महिनाको अप्रेन्टिससिप हो, स्थायी बैंक जागिर होइन — यो कुरा बुझेर मात्र आवेदन दिनु राम्रो हुन्छ।</p>
<h2>एक नजरमा</h2>
<table><tr><th>विवरण</th><td>जानकारी</td></tr><tr><td>संस्था</td><td>इन्डियन बैंक, सार्वजनिक क्षेत्रको बैंक, मुख्यालय चेन्नई</td></tr><tr><td>पद</td><td>अप्रेन्टिस</td></tr><tr><td>कुल पद</td><td>१,५०० (अस्थायी)</td></tr><tr><td>आवेदन मिति</td><td>५ देखि २५ नोभेम्बर २०२६</td></tr><tr><td>आवेदन माध्यम</td><td>एनएटीएस २.० पोर्टल (nats.education.gov.in)</td></tr><tr><td>योग्यता</td><td>कुनै पनि विषयमा स्नातक, १ अप्रिल २०२२ वा त्यसपछि र १ नोभेम्बर २०२६ भन्दा ढिला नभई उत्तीर्ण</td></tr><tr><td>उमेर</td><td>१ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा २० देखि २८ वर्ष</td></tr><tr><td>मासिक भत्ता</td><td>महानगर र सहरी शाखामा १५,०००; ग्रामीण र अर्ध-सहरी शाखामा १२,३०० भारतीय रुपैयाँ</td></tr><tr><td>तालिम अवधि</td><td>१२ महिना</td></tr><tr><td>आवेदन शुल्क</td><td>सामान्यका लागि ८०० रुपैयाँ थप जीएसटी; एससी, एसटी र पीडब्ल्यूबीडीका लागि १७५ रुपैयाँ थप जीएसटी</td></tr><tr><td>छनोट</td><td>अनलाइन परीक्षा, त्यसपछि स्थानीय भाषा परीक्षा</td></tr></table>
<h2>को योग्य छ</h2>
<p>कुनै पनि विषयमा स्नातक गरेकाले आवेदन दिन सक्छन्, तर स्नातकको मिति डिग्रीभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण छ। १ अप्रिल २०२२ वा त्यसपछि र १ नोभेम्बर २०२६ भन्दा ढिला नभई स्नातक उत्तीर्ण भएको हुनुपर्छ, र अन्तिम नतिजा १ नोभेम्बर २०२६ सम्ममा प्रकाशित भएको हुनुपर्छ। २०२१ मा स्नातक गरेकाले आवेदन दिन सक्दैनन्। उमेर १ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा २० देखि २८ वर्ष हुनुपर्छ, अर्थात् जन्ममिति २ नोभेम्बर १९९८ देखि १ नोभेम्बर २००६ बीच हुनुपर्छ। एससी र एसटीका लागि ५ वर्ष, ओबीसी नन-क्रिमिलेयरका लागि ३ वर्ष र पीडब्ल्यूबीडीका लागि १० वर्षसम्म उमेर छुट छ।</p>
<p>पहिले नै अप्रेन्टिससिप गरिसकेका, अहिले गरिरहेका वा बीचमा छोडेकाले आवेदन दिन सक्दैनन्। योग्यता पूरा गरेपछि एक वर्ष वा सोभन्दा बढी काम गरेको अनुभव भएकालाई पनि अयोग्य मानिन्छ। एउटा राज्य वा केन्द्रशासित प्रदेशका लागि मात्र आवेदन दिन पाइन्छ। उत्तर प्रदेशमा सबैभन्दा धेरै २८५, तमिलनाडुमा २७० र पश्चिम बंगालमा १४५ पद छन्।</p>
<h2>परीक्षा र आवेदन कसरी गर्ने</h2>
<p>छनोट दुई चरणमा हुन्छ। पहिलो चरणमा १०० प्रश्नको अनलाइन वस्तुगत परीक्षा हुन्छ — १०० अंक, ६० मिनेट। तर्कशक्ति १५, कम्प्युटर ज्ञान १०, अंग्रेजी २५, परिमाणात्मक योग्यता २५ र बैंकिङसम्बन्धी सामान्य ज्ञान २५ प्रश्न छन्। कुनै एउटा खण्डमा न्यूनतम अंक तोकिएको छैन; बैंकले तोकेको कुल न्यूनतम अंक ल्याउनुपर्छ। मेरिट सूची राज्य र श्रेणीअनुसार बन्छ, बराबरी भएमा ठूलो उमेरकालाई प्राथमिकता दिइन्छ। विज्ञापनमा परीक्षाको मिति तोकिएको छैन — बैंकले आफ्नो वेबसाइटमा ननिकालेसम्म कुनै मितिलाई विश्वास नगर्नुहोस्।</p>
<p>दोस्रो चरण स्थानीय भाषा प्रवीणता परीक्षा हो। आवेदन दिएको राज्यको तोकिएको स्थानीय भाषा पढ्न, लेख्न, बोल्न र बुझ्न सक्नुपर्छ। ८औं, १०औं वा १२औं कक्षाको मार्कसिटमा त्यो भाषा पढेको देखिएमा यो परीक्षा दिनु पर्दैन। पहिले एनएटीएस २.० पोर्टलमा विद्यार्थीका रूपमा दर्ता गरेर प्रोफाइल १०० प्रतिशत पूरा गर्नुहोस्, त्यसपछि इन्डियन बैंकको अप्रेन्टिस पदमा आवेदन दिनुहोस्। एनएटीएस खाता बनाउनु मात्रै आवेदन होइन — तोकिएको रिक्त पदमा आवेदन दिनैपर्छ।</p>
<h2>भत्ता र सावधानी</h2>
<p>महानगर र सहरी शाखामा मासिक भत्ता १५,००० र ग्रामीण तथा अर्ध-सहरी शाखामा १२,३०० भारतीय रुपैयाँ छ। महानगरमा बैंकले ८,८५० र सरकारले ६,१५० रुपैयाँ दिन्छ; ग्रामीणमा दुवैले ६,१५० रुपैयाँ दिन्छन्। यसबाहेक अन्य कुनै भत्ता वा सुविधा छैन। १२ महिनामा ३३८ भन्दा बढी भुक्तानी भएका दिन पूरा गरेपछि मात्र दक्षता प्रमाणपत्र पाइन्छ। अप्रेन्टिसहरू बैंकका कर्मचारी होइनन्; तालिम सकिएपछि बैंकले नियमित जागिर दिनुपर्ने कुनै दायित्व छैन। त्यसैले यो वर्षलाई तलबसहितको तालिमका रूपमा हेर्नुहोस् — स्थायी जागिरको पछाडिको बाटोका रूपमा होइन। आवेदन आधिकारिक एनएटीएस पोर्टल र बैंकको करिअर पेजबाट मात्र दिनुहोस्, र जागिर दिलाइदिन्छु भन्दै पैसा माग्ने जोकोहीबाट सावधान रहनुहोस्।</p>
<p><small>स्रोत: इन्डियन बैंक, आर्थिक वर्ष २०२६–२७ का लागि अप्रेन्टिस नियुक्तिसम्बन्धी अन्तिम अद्यावधिक विज्ञापन, ४ नोभेम्बर २०२६; JobCareerUpdates र Testbook मा प्रकाशित विवरण। आवेदन nats.education.gov.in बाट मात्र दिनुहोस्।</small></p>
